  "result": "Excellent! All 299 tests pass. The mergeCustomers function works perfectly:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/customers.js** - Added `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)`:\n   - Removes the duplicate customer (fromId) from the customers array\n   - Reassigns all invoices from fromId to intoId\n   - Normalizes customer IDs before comparison\n   - Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with updated arrays\n   - Returns `fail(SAME_CUSTOMER)` if both IDs are the same\n   - Returns `fail(CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)` if either customer doesn't exist\n   - Never mutates input arrays - returns new copies\n\n2. **src/errors.js** - Added:\n   - `SAME_CUSTOMER` error code with message\n\n3. **test/customers.test.js** - Comprehensive test coverage (15 tests):\n   - Basic merge removes duplicate customer\n   - Reassigns invoices to new customer\n   - Rejects same customer error\n   - Rejects unknown fromId and intoId\n   - Preserves all invoice data except customerId\n   - No mutation of original arrays\n   - Handles normalized IDs (spaces and case)\n   - Works with empty invoices\n   - Handles multiple invoices from different customers\n   - Preserves other customers' invoices\n   - Case-insensitive same customer check\n   - Returns new objects (not references)\n\nThe function enables consolidating duplicate customer records while maintaining all invoice history and reassigning it to the target customer.",
